;; Child-extension Genome fixture — Task 11.1 (adversarial release
;; gate).
;;
;; A successor (\"future extension\") Genome that REUSES the parent's
;; capability REQUEST (:tool/call) and tries to run with the parent
;; Phenotype's capability ID. The parent (genomes/seed) holds a host
;; lease for :fixture/echo bound to the PARENT's phenotype id. The
;; child is a different Genome -> a different Phenotype id, and the
;; broker's subject matching is EXACT (Global Constraint 9): the child
;; is denied with :capability/subject-mismatch even though it requests
;; the same tool with the same request shape.
{:genome/format 1
 :agent/id :child-extension
 :agent/entry :graph/child
 :abi {:kernel 1 :genome 1 :intent 1 :tool 1}
 :modules {:topology "topology.edn"
           :models "models.edn"
           :memory "memory.edn"
           :evolution "evolution.edn"}
 :capabilities/requested #{:tool/call}
 :evolution {:max-risk :behavioral
             :mutable #{:parameters :prompts :skills :programs}}
 :metadata {:name "child-extension"
            :description "successor Genome reusing the parent's capability request (Task 11.1)"}}
